BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 625.87 Tm (operating_framework) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 603.65 Tm (Score evidence, not optimism. Use a 100-point intake model: 25 points for enforceability and standing, 25 for verified) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 588.42 Tm (debtor-owned assets, 20 for residual value after senior claims and exemptions, 15 for executable venue and procedure,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 573.20 Tm (and 15 for creditor economics and cooperation. Require 75 points for a paid investigation proposal and 85 for a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 557.97 Tm (recovery proposal; these are internal triage thresholds, not measured success probabilities. An active bankruptcy stay,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 542.75 Tm (disputed authority, an expired judgment, or unresolved licensing requirements overrides any score. Separate evidence) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 527.52 Tm (into confirmed facts, dated third-party records, and hypotheses requiring verification. A screenshot of a successful) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 512.30 Tm (business does not earn asset points without ownership support. Request the entered judgment, relevant orders, service) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 497.07 Tm (history where material, assignments, payment ledger, current counsel details, and prior enforcement invoices. Check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 481.85 Tm (renewal and limitation rules in the actual enforcing jurisdiction. Interest calculations must follow the applicable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 466.62 Tm (judgment and law, including payment credits; do not apply a favorite percentage universally. Under Federal Rule of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 451.40 Tm (Civil Procedure 69, federal money-judgment execution generally uses state procedure unless a federal statute applies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 436.17 Tm (That procedural bridge makes local counsel and jurisdiction-specific checklists more valuable than a national template) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 420.95 Tm (claiming universal coverage.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 405.72 Tm (Build a priority waterfall before estimating the operator's fee. Suppose a commercial asset could realize $150,000,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 390.50 Tm (documented sale and enforcement costs total $15,000, and senior claims consume $110,000. Only $25,000 remains) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 375.27 Tm (before other applicable claims or exemptions. A $100,000 judgment does not turn that $25,000 residual into $100,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 360.05 Tm (of collectible value. If the engagement permits a 35% service fee on recovered funds, the illustrative fee ceiling is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 344.82 Tm ($8,750, not $35,000. Order UCC searches in the relevant filing jurisdiction, check county records where appropriate,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 329.60 Tm (and have counsel reconcile lien attachment, perfection, priority, and execution timing. A lapsed financing statement is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 314.37 Tm (not proof that the underlying debt vanished or that your creditor automatically moved ahead. Likewise, a tax lien search) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 299.15 Tm (does not replace reviewing the governing priority rules. Screen bankruptcy using official records at intake and again) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 283.92 Tm (before enforcement. Section 362 of title 11 can halt collection acts, and section 524 can prohibit collection of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 268.70 Tm (discharged personal liability. A dismissal, closing, or discharge entry needs order-specific interpretation. Where) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 253.47 Tm (ownership or priority remains contested, cap investigation spending and obtain a written legal assessment before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 238.25 Tm (proposing an asset-specific recovery timeline to the creditor.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 223.02 Tm (Set an investigation budget using expected contribution, with explicit uncertainty. For a file with $20,000 estimated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 207.80 Tm (collectible proceeds, a 35% fee would produce $7,000 if collected. At an illustrative 40% collection probability,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 192.57 Tm (expected fee revenue is $2,800. Subtract $500 acquisition cost and $900 expected unreimbursed investigation and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 177.35 Tm (enforcement expense to leave $1,400 before shared overhead and timing effects. This calculation is a screening model,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 162.12 Tm (not a valuation of the judgment or an instruction to purchase it. Stress the probability to 20%; expected contribution) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 146.90 Tm (then falls to zero under the same assumptions. Prefer files whose downside remains manageable after such a stress.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 131.67 Tm (Document whether court costs are advanced by the creditor, recovered from proceeds, absorbed by the operator, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 116.45 Tm (separately billed by counsel. Never count the same reimbursement twice. Use staged authority: initial document review,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 101.22 Tm (bounded asset investigation, then counsel-selected enforcement. Limit personal data to what the authorized task needs,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 86.00 Tm (and restrict access by role. Public availability does not authorize impersonation, pretexting for bank information, or) Tj ET
